                <pb facs="1071" n="961" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg961"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">667.003/274: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Angora</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-12T15:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                                1928—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 12—1:30
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>10. It now appears improbable that the new Turkish tariff law will be passed
                    before March or April at earliest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
